      excerpt: `A credit equal to the applicable percentage of so much of the qualified retirement savings contributions of the eligible individual\u2026 as do not exceed $2,000 \u2014 per individual (spouse separately on a joint return). ${tableExcerpt} Head-of-household tiers are 75 percent and all other statuses 50 percent of the joint amounts (\xA7 25B(b)(2)) \u2014 a surviving-spouse return is not a joint return, so the "all other" tiers apply. Ineligible: full-time students and claimed dependents (\xA7 25B(c)(2)); attainment of age 18 (\xA7 25B(c)(1)) is assumed \u2014 disclosed. Contributions are net of \xA7 25B(d)(2) testing-period distributions \u2014 attested by the input. [For taxable years after 2026 the credit is replaced by the \xA7 6433 Saver's Match (SECURE 2.0 \xA7 103; OBBBA \xA7 70116).]`
