      source: `26 U.S.C. \xA7\xA7 901, 904, 960(d)${version > 1 ? ", as amended by Pub. L. 119-21 (OBBBA)" : ""}`,
      section: "\xA7 904(a), (d); \xA7 960(d)",
      url: "https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/26/904",
      excerpt: `Foreign taxes credited up to the \xA7 904 limitation per basket \u2014 the US tax multiplied by the basket's foreign-source taxable income over total taxable income (net of \xA7 250). The \xA7 951A-basket deemed-paid credit is limited to ${haircutLabel} of the foreign taxes (\xA7 960(d)), and that basket's income is net of its allocable \xA7 250 deduction; no carryovers exist in the \xA7 951A basket, and the general basket's 1-back/10-forward carryovers are not tracked \u2014 disclosed. [Two baskets modeled (general + CFC); the foreign-branch and passive baskets, \xA7 861 expense allocation, and \xA7 78 fine structure are attested by the inputs.]`
